[{"id":4407675853,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBrfLzQ","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?u=b7882c94f408976a2f79e8fe6e1ce27fbd48db74&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The approach taken here does not work for a dynamic call:\n\n```gdscript\n@abstract class T extends RefCounted:\n\tpass\n\nvar a: Variant = T\n\nfunc _run() -> void:\n    print(a.can_instantiate())\n    print(a.new())\n```\n\nThis still produces an object (although not an instance of the script). `CALL_ERROR_INVALID_METHOD` falls back to calling on the native class which creates a `RefCounted` instance in this case.\n\nI'm also not sure about this returning an error method thing. This works when using the methodbind from the GDScriptVM. But couldn't it mess up extensions?","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119932#pullrequestreview-4407675853","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119932","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pu